":"NOASSERTION","url":null,"node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTA="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"has_pull_requests":true,"pull_request_creation_policy":"all","topics":["autograd","deep-learning","gpu","machine-learning","neural-network","numpy","python","tensor"],"visibility":"public","forks":27143,"open_issues":18135,"watchers":98201,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"### 🐛 Describe the bug\r\n\r\nTest on the CPU:\r\n\r\n    import torch\r\n    input = torch.randn(3)\r\n    out = torch.triu(input)\r\n    print(out)\r\n\r\nresult: IndexError: Dimension out of range (expected to be in range of [-1, 0], but got -2)\r\n\r\nTest on the GPU:\r\n\r\n    import torch\r\n    input = torch.randn(3).cuda()\r\n    out = torch.triu(input)\r\n    print(out)\r\n\r\nresult: tensor([-0.2992,  1.0819,  1.2671], device='cuda:0')\r\n\r\ntorch.triu suggested that the input we input is a two-dimensional tensor, but when I deliberately used a one-dimensional tensor to test, I found that it failed on the CPU, but succeeded on the GPU.The same happens with the torch.tril operator.\r\n\r\n\r\n### Versions\r\n\r\npytorch: 1.12.1\r\nPython version: 3.8\r\nCUDA/cuDNN version: cuDNN 11.3\r\nGPU models and configuration: RTX3060\r\nOperating System：Windows","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/89400/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/89400/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"id":7862219401,"node_id":"CE_lADOA-j9z85Ps8L8zwAAAAHUn_KJ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/events/7862219401","actor":{"login":"pytorchmergebot","id":97764156,"node_id":"U_kgDOBdPDPA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubu